<Base
  title="TOPLAP Strasbourg charter"
  description="Values and ground rules of the TOPLAP Strasbourg association: openness, sharing, experimentation, community."
>
  <p style="font-size:0.82rem;margin-bottom:1.2rem">
    <a href="/en/ressources">← Resources</a>
  </p>

  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>TOPLAP Strasbourg charter</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--muted)">What we stand for, and how we want to share our events, workshops and spaces together.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="doc-section" style="border-bottom:none">
    <h2>Our values</h2>

    <h3>Openness and accessibility</h3>
    <p>Live coding and digital arts should be accessible to everyone, whatever their level. We never assume you need to "already know how to code" to join us: our workshops are designed so you can come in through music, visuals, or plain curiosity.</p>

    <h3>Sharing and free culture</h3>
    <p>In the spirit of the international TOPLAP network, we encourage sharing knowledge, tools and source code. What gets made at our events is meant to circulate: code published, recordings shared, know-how documented rather than kept to ourselves.</p>

    <h3>Creation and experimentation</h3>
    <p>We support artistic research and innovation in the digital arts. Errors, bugs and crashes are part of the game — a performance that goes wrong is not a failure, it's a risk taken on purpose.</p>

    <h3>Community</h3>
    <p>We bring together an open, caring and collaborative collective. Nobody plays alone: artists, technicians, audience — everyone contributes to what happens in the room.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" style="border-bottom:none">
    <h2>Ground rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Respect.</strong> No discriminatory, harassing or disrespectful behaviour is tolerated, towards anyone — artist, volunteer, audience. This applies online (Discord, social media) as much as in the room.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent.</strong> Ask before filming, photographing or recording anyone recognisable. Respect a "no" without argument.</li>
      <li><strong>Show your code.</strong> "Show us your screens" — in the TOPLAP spirit, we don't hide what we're running. Transparency is a courtesy to the audience as much as an aesthetic principle.</li>
      <li><strong>Take care of equipment and venues.</strong> Our events take place in venues that host us (Le Shadok, La Pérestroïka, La Grenze, Karmen Camina, Diamant d'Or...). We leave them the way we found them.</li>
      <li><strong>Pay what you can, DIY spirit.</strong> Many of our events are pay-what-you-want. Contribute according to your means, and keep in mind that this way of working relies on the group's solidarity.</li>
      <li><strong>Give credit.</strong> Mention the people whose code, visuals or tools you use. It goes hand in hand with the free culture we stand for.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" style="border-bottom:none">
    <h2>A problem, a conflict?</h2>
    <p>If something isn't right during an event or in our online spaces, you can talk to any board member or reach us through the <a href="/en/contact">contact</a> page. We'd much rather hear about it early than find out about a problem afterwards.</p>
  </section>

  <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted)">This text evolves with the association — suggestions welcome.</p>
</Base>
